      "documentSlug": "care-partner-support-and-caregiver-burden-in-pd",
      "documentConcept": "Care partner support and caregiver burden in PD",
      "canonicalConceptId": "concept:3b245dd6feca8251e90824479bdf5ab246908953d37241b10113f2f7cb48d6dd",
      "text": "Care partners provide emotional and practical support in PD while facing risks to their own health, social lives and finances. Evidence supports assessing their needs separately, providing tailored information, and arranging practical help, time away and suitable peer support. Neuropsychiatric difficulties, functional impact and caregiver mental health are relevant to burden, but predictors vary by study method. Small psychological and educational studies report benefits in selected domains; pooled findings and other outcomes are less consistent. Resource recommendations should therefore be distinguished from proven treatment effects, and care plans tailored to the relationship and available support.",
